    "medium_raw": "Lacquered (Burmese. thitsi) and gilded paper and card with thayo (relief ornament) and hman-zi shwei-cha (shaped  lamin or coloured looking glass inlay). The paper is made from the pulped bark of Paper Mulberry Tree (Latin.  Broussonetia papyrifera).",
    "classification": "Folding Manuscript",
    "styles": [
      "Konbaung"
    ],
    "categories": [],
    "physical_description": "Folding manuscript (Burmese. parabaik). The pages are uncoloured and the text is written in black Burmese round  script. The borders of the pages are illuminated. The cover of the manuscript is lacquered and gilded relief moulded  (Burmese. thayo) card with glass inlay (Burmese. hman-zi shwei-cha) and foliate decorative motifs.\r\n\r\nThe title on the front cover translates to \"Song in glorification of the Holy and High Buddha.\" The manuscript is  understood to be a volume of verses (Burmese. ei-gyin) extolling the glorious achievements of past ancestors of the Konbaung Dynastyy as well as cradle songs, music and eulogies to be recited and sung to the eldest daughter of King Thibaw and Queen Supayalat on the occasion of piercing her ears 10th day after in the Burmese year 1243 (1882).",
    "summary": null,
    "historical_context": null,
    "dimensions": [],
    "dimensions_note": null,
    "marks_inscriptions": null
  },
